# Credential shape for bases-mcp.
//
// The runtime shape for every variable the binary reads lives at the repository
// root in `.env.schema`; this file is the DEPLOYMENT's credential shape — the
// four vault variables the renderer requests as podman secrets. It does not
// duplicate the transport or audit variables, which are set in `compose.yaml`.
// Names, types and examples; never a value.
//
// The vault is chosen by the environment: `BASES_MCP_VAULT` names a vault
// mounted into the container, `BASES_MCP_WEBDAV_*` a remote one. Exactly one
// backend is used, and `BASES_MCP_VAULT` wins if both are set. These are the
// variables an operator must plant; the renderer requests them as podman secrets
// and they arrive as environment variables (BASES_MCP_*, read by the binary).
//
// Production connects to OxiCloud (WebDAV), not rustfs: the WebDAV trio is the
// required backend there. `BASES_MCP_VAULT` (the filesystem backend) is left
// optional so a local/scratch deploy can still use it.

// @defaultSensitive=true
// @defaultRequired=false

// BASES_MCP_VAULT
//   @sensitive
//   @required false
//   @type env
//   @example /vault

// BASES_MCP_WEBDAV_URL
//   @sensitive
//   @required true
//   @type env
//   @example https://cloud.kroeppl.online/webdav/

// BASES_MCP_WEBDAV_USER
//   @sensitive
//   @required true
//   @type env
//   @auditIgnore

// BASES_MCP_WEBDAV_PASSWORD
//   @sensitive
//   @required true
//   @type env
//   @auditIgnore
